 //
+//  ErrorBoundary   wraps ONE screen (the tab bar stays usable).
+//  RootBoundary    wraps the WHOLE app. Without it, anything thrown above the
+//                  screen (the app shell, a provider) would leave the person on a
+//                  blank white page with no way back — which is what a phone shows
+//                  when a React tree is torn down. It renders FatalScreen instead.
